1" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"394"></span>
<p></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"columnLayout fixed-width" data-layout=3D"fixed-width">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-not=
e">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-warning confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>There is a 1,000-character limit on the value of variables set in Logic+=
.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #C0B6F2;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #C0B6F2;">
<p>To return data to Classic Logic, dotCX, and action bots, you can use the=
 Set Variable Panel and a variable naming convention of 'SharpenCX_ClassicL=
ogic_&lt;varName&gt;'. The Classic Logic flow will have access to a call va=
riable named &lt;varName&gt;.</p>
</div>
</div>
<p>Related Article: <a href=3D"https://sharpencx.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/=
CT1/pages/4231364609/Available+Predefined+Variables" data-linked-resource-i=
d=3D"4231364609" data-linked-resource-version=3D"18" data-linked-resource-t=
ype=3D"page">Available Predefined Variables</a></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
    </div>
</body>
